.TH CHTTPSVR_ROUTER_ON_STREAM 3 "2026-08-03" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_router_on_stream \- register a streaming handler on a sub-router
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_router_on_stream(chttpsvr_router *router,
                                         chttp_method_t method,
                                         const char *pattern,
                                         chttpsvr_handler_fn fn,
                                         void *ctx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
The same as chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler, except that the
route goes on a sub-router.  The pattern rules of
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler apply here too: pattern must
start with '/', a {name} segment must contain only [A-Za-z0-9_], and
the same {name} must not appear more than once.  CHTTP_ANY works as
the method argument as well.  The handler runs on the streaming pool
of the server, exactly like a handler registered with
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler.

The function first checks that the server that owns router has not
been destroyed.  That check also holds against a destroy running on
another thread at the same time: a call that races a chttpsvr_destroy
of the owning server returns ccol_invalid_args and touches no freed
memory.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args when router, pattern or fn is NULL; when method is
                  not one of the seven methods or CHTTP_ANY; when
                  pattern does not start with '/'; when pattern has two
                  consecutive slashes or a trailing slash; when a
                  {name} segment contains a character outside
                  [A-Za-z0-9_]; when the same {name} appears more than
                  once; or when the server that owns router has been
                  destroyed.
ccol_not_enough_memory when an allocation fails.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler (3),
.BR chttpsvr_subrouter (3)
